{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85","name":"Speed","source":{"id":"source:reference-c372fee9b4566b85","title":"Speed","revision":18519,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:15:08Z","sha256":"b5df9e500eea7bbd8bbe100e3e95fdd4049e89382be5e9336af018624f42e209","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18519","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Speed&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c372fee9b4566b85","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Your Speed tells you how far you can ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move","referenceId":"reference:6ecc3df6bffdd06c"}," with a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},". Your Speed depends mostly on your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", although certain kinds of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"}," can reduce your Speed. Some creatures, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," have a natural Climb, Burrow, Fly, and/or Swim Speed in addition to their normal Walking Speed. Any effect that reduces Speed affects all of a creature's movement modes unless noted otherwise. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Moving Diagonally costs double. When ",{"tag":"a","children":["Moving"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Moving"}," or counting along a diagonal path, each diagonal step counts as 2 squares. If a character moves diagonally through ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low Objects"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low_Objects"}," or Difficult Terrain, the cost of movement doubles twice (that is, each square counts as 4 squares).\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Character Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Speed is measured in Squares. Each Square represents 1.5 meters (about 5 feet).\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Encumbrance"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Wearing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Medium Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Medium_Armor","referenceId":"reference:e2a45d7d144d40dd"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Armor","referenceId":"reference:4bc2d20a5687b54f"}," or carrying a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Load"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Load"}," reduces your character's Speed to three-quarters normal (4 squares if your Base Speed is 6 squares, or 3 squares if your Base Speed is 4 squares).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["While wearing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Armor","referenceId":"reference:4bc2d20a5687b54f"}," or carrying a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Load"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Load"},", you can only ",{"tag":"a","children":["Run"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Run","referenceId":"reference:00d60e31a4e6b834"}," at triple your Speed (instead of quadruple).\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Flight"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A creature with a Fly Speed is capable of flight, but not if carrying a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Load"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Load"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Vehicle Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Every ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," has a Speed, given in squares. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," may move up to its listed Speed as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},", and up to four times its Speed with the ",{"tag":"a","children":["All-Out Movement"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/All-Out_Movement","referenceId":"reference:c3e269326f94373b"}," Action. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"}," have a separate listing for their Speed in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Maximum Velocity"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["This is the maximum Speed a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," may move in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Character_Scale"},". It is seldom relevant in combat, because such speeds quickly move the vessel off the battle map, and out of range.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Mass Combat"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Every ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"}," has a Speed, given in squares. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Field Commander"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Field_Commander","referenceId":"reference:5ad8d1c0fe6dab83"}," can move a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"}," up to its listed Speed as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},", and up to four times its Speed with the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hard March"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hard_March"}," Action. All Speeds are listed in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},". For the most part, all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," based on creatures or characters have a ground Speed of 1. Battalions with the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Battalion Template"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Battalion_Template?action=edit&redlink=1"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mounted Battalion Template"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mounted_Battalion_Template?action=edit&redlink=1"}," might move faster.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Vehicle Speed"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Some ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", particularly ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ground Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ground_Vehicles"},", do not have a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," Speed. Use the table below to determine the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," Speed of any Battalions that do not have such a Speed listed.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHARACTER SCALE SPEED\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["STARSHIP SCALE SPEED\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0-11 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1 Square\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["12-15 Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["16+ Squares\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3 Squares\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Diagonal Movement"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Moving"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Moving"}," diagonally costs double. When Moving or counting along a diagonal path, each diagonal step counts as 2 squares. If a character moves diagonally through ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low Objects"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low_Objects"}," or Difficult Terrain, the cost of movement doubles twice (that is, each square counts as 4 squares). A character can't make Diagonal Movement past the corner or end of a wall that extends to a grid center.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Difficult Terrain"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Broken ground, buckled deck plating, and similar obstacles are collectively referred to as Difficult Terrain. It costs twice as much to move into a square containing Difficult Terrain. Creatures of Large size and bigger must pay the extra cost for moving across Difficult Terrain if any part of their Fighting Space moves into such a square. Difficult Terrain does not block ",{"tag":"a","children":["Line of Sight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Line_of_Sight","referenceId":"reference:7ae5eaf79143552f"}," or provide ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cover"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cover"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Immobilized"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When a creature is Immobilized it cannot move by its own volition. An Immobilized creature can take ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Actions"},", but it cannot ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move","referenceId":"reference:6ecc3df6bffdd06c"}," from its current space, and it cannot make ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Checks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Checks"}," associated with movement (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Climb"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Climb","referenceId":"reference:98ca5f27d9642dc7"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jump"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jump","referenceId":"reference:9ee0ca3e24d60ea0"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swim","referenceId":"reference:dd4fa375c70c4e42"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["An Immobilized creature can still be moved by other effects, such as being the target of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bantha Rush"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bantha_Rush","referenceId":"reference:538eb665ec0bd30c"}," or the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Thrust"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Thrust","referenceId":"reference:71dad1bff9398936"}]}," Force Power.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
